# Hermes ignore list — paths the drop-zone indexer must never walk or quote.
#
# ⚠️ Read this before trusting it: `.hermesignore` is NOT a Hermes Agent feature.
# It was proposed in upstream issues (NousResearch/hermes-agent #502, #681, #50165)
# and as of 2026-09-21 a code search for "hermesignore" in that repo returns 0 hits.
# So Hermes itself ignores this file — the CPU win described in 2026-06-02/summary.md
# came from nothing more than placing it in the workspace root.
#
# What it does do: it is the single source of truth for `scripts/hermes-index.sh`
# (which builds the small `INDEX.md` that Hermes reads instead of walking ~400k files)
# and for the container's own view of the drop zone. That is the mechanism that
# actually keeps the system prompt small.
#
# Syntax: one path-segment name or glob per line, matched against directory/file
# basenames while walking. Blank lines and `#` comments ignored.

# --- dependencies / package caches (the 400k-file offenders) ---
node_modules/
bower_components/
vendor/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.tox/
.nox/
.pnpm-store/
.uv-cache/
.site-packages/

# --- VCS + tooling state ---
.git/
.git-object-store/
.svn/
.hg/
.vscode/
.idea/
.nx/
.turbo/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/
.next/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage/

# --- build outputs ---
dist/
build/
out/
target/
obj/
Debug/
Release/
site-packages/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.map
*.woff2
*.ttf
*.pdf
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.gz
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.mp4
*.mov
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- secrets: never indexed, never quoted, never summarised ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials
credentials.json
service-account*.json
.secrets
.netrc
npm-debug.log*

# --- noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
*.tmp
tmp/
coverage/
htmlcov/
.coverage
